# The B0xx certification work streams keep their SOURCES in a directory named
# "build", which the blanket build-output rules above would swallow. Those
# sources are declared by the CMake targets, so a fresh checkout without them
# cannot even configure: CMake reports "Cannot find source file" for a path
# that plainly exists in the maintainer's tree. The sources are tracked here;
# the build outputs that share the directory are not.
!B0*/build/
B0*/build/*
!B0*/build/*.cpp
!B0*/build/*.c
!B0*/build/*.cc
!B0*/build/*.h
!B0*/build/*.hpp
!B0*/build/*.inc
!B0*/build/*.asm
!B0*/build/*.py
!B0*/build/*.ps1
!B0*/build/*.bat
